  "body": "## Versions\n\n`vize` **0.593.0** (npm), Node 26.6.0, macOS arm64.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nRepro directory: `repro/xf-script-offset/`.\n\n`src/App.vue`\n\n```vue\n<script lang=\"ts\">\nexport const label = \"settings\";\n</script>\n\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { provide } from \"vue\";\nimport Child from \"./Child.vue\";\n\nprovide(\"theme\", \"dark\");\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <Child />\n</template>\n```\n\n`src/Child.vue`\n\n```vue\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">\nimport { inject } from \"vue\";\n\nconst theme = inject(\"theme\");\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <p>{{ theme }}</p>\n</template>\n```\n\n```\n$ vize lint -f plain --no-config --cross-file \"src/**/*.vue\" | grep App.vue\n  src/App.vue:7:1 warning cross-file vize:croquis/cf/non-reactive-provide: provide('theme') value is not reactive - consumers won't see updates\n  src/App.vue:7:1 warning cross-file vize:croquis/cf/provide-without-symbol: provide('theme') uses a string injection key; …\n```\n\n`provide(\"theme\", \"dark\")` is at **9:1**; 7:1 is the `import Child …` line.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The shift is the distance between the end of the plain `<script>` content and the start of the `<script setup>`\n  content, minus one: here `</script>\\n\\n<script setup lang=\"ts\">` is 35 characters and the position is 34 characters\n  early. Adding `generic=\"T\"` to the `<script setup>` tag moves the reported position 12 characters further back\n  (6:20). It looks like the offset into \"plain script + `\\n` + setup script\" is mapped from the start of the plain\n  script block.\n- Template positions (`duplicate-id`) in the same SFCs are right, and so are the ordinary (non-cross-file) rules.\n- Any SFC that keeps imports or exports in a plain `<script>` block is affected, so the reported line points at an\n  unrelated statement (on a larger file it was 4 lines and a different `inject()` early), and a line-level directive\n  could not be placed by the reported line either.\n\n## Expected\n\n`src/App.vue:9:1` for both diagnostics.\n",
